+    // DS4_CACHE_ROUTE=b (fast-routing patch; CHANGES THE ANSWERS; unset or 0 = off): cache-aware routing on the
+    // decode path.  Each layer's routing bias (the number route_kernel adds to an expert's score only to choose the top
+    // k; the pick's weight still comes from its unbiased score) gets +b for every expert that needs no SSD read now: in
+    // VRAM (slot), in the RAM tier, or ready in the RAM store (--ssd-cache).  A cold expert then loses a close call to
+    // a warm one; a clear winner still wins.  Related: Mixture of Cache-Conditional Experts (arXiv 2412.00099) and
+    // Edge0's prediction-as-routing (arXiv 2609.18063), here for DeepSeek, without training.  Scores are
+    // sqrt(softplus(logit)), about 0.5 to 3, so b is a small number: 0.02 to 0.1 to try.
+    //   DS4_CACHE_ROUTE_EVERY=n (4): the warm sets are looked at, and changed layers' biases uploaded, every n tokens
+    //   DS4_CACHE_ROUTE_FROM=l (0): only layers from l on
+    //   DS4_CACHE_ROUTE_LOG=1: a line per request with the uploads and the warm share of the CPU lane's picks
+    //   DS4_CACHE_ROUTE_VRAM=v (0): an extra +v for experts in VRAM (they skip the CPU lane's expert math as well)
+    //   DS4_CACHE_ROUTE_STICKY=s (0): an extra +s for the experts this layer picked for the previous word (words
+    //     reuse experts; it also makes the lookahead's guesses land).  With s > 0 the biases are refreshed every word.
+    //   DS4_CACHE_ROUTE_CTL=file: "b v s" (three numbers) read before each request, replacing the three values, so a
+    //     bench or a front end can change them without a reload (a missing or bad file changes nothing)
+    // Prompts (chunks and prompt windows) route with the unmodified biases: the bonus is taken out before them.
